        "email": "tbrasselle@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T14:45:22Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(multiaxis): the Rotary Flow multi-band and single-helix kernel\n\nThe picked guide chains read as ONE ordered set (#2829), in a new\nrotary_flow_set module of the motion crate:\n\n- three or more ordered chains machine one band per adjacent pair,\n  and the SHARED boundary chain is cut once - band k > 0 starts at\n  its first interior pass;\n- a single chain machines the full revolution: the kernel morphs it\n  to its own next lap (th + TAU in the unwrap's own reading), the\n  developed band is exactly one revolution wide, and the lap's\n  closing pass is dropped because the lap's two edges are one world\n  curve;\n- a chain wound against its pair is walked backwards (the feature\n  layer reads a chain's direction from the mesh, never from the\n  pick) - superseding #2824's opposite-sense refusal, said in the\n  notes;\n- chains that meet or cross are refused by name at the shared spot\n  (the exact segment-pair law), and bands that double back through\n  the chain before them are refused as a set out of band order.\n\nThe app wiring needed no change: the picks already ride the chains\ninto the kernel. App-level pins on the turned bar: three ring chains\ncut two bands with the boundary once; one meridian chain machines\nthe full revolution (19 passes, one landing per azimuth); the\nmeridian-plus-ring set refuses at the shared corner.\n\nFixes #2829",
