      "message": "fix(multiaxis): normalize the guide set once and refuse the ring lap\n\nTwo blocking findings of the PR #4018 review, both closed by a law\nover the complete input:\n\n- The winding of each guide is resolved ONCE against its\n  pair-neighbour before any band is cut, and the same normalized\n  track bounds both adjacent bands. A band-by-band reversal on a\n  clone left the next band's lower boundary at the raw winding, so a\n  set with only its middle pick reversed flipped the cutting\n  direction of the second band without a change to climb. Pinned\n  pass by pass, both climb settings.\n- A single guide that turns at one axial station and one radius -\n  a closed ring or an open arc of one - is refused by name before a\n  pass is generated. Its lap reads a positive angular width but\n  sweeps no band area: the family repeated one closed cut.\n\nThe non-adjacent crossing the review named non-blocking is filed as\n#4032.\n\nFixes #2829",
